    "result": "I rewrote `solution.py` to fix both failed gates, and the 8 tests still pass. I haven't re-run the gates themselves, so the CRAP and mutation results are unconfirmed.\n\n- **CRAP:** `check_password` now just validates the types and then runs a table of five rule functions, one per rule code. That brings its complexity down to about 3, well under the CRAP limit.\n- **Mutation:** the character-class logic now uses `string` constants and `in` checks instead of range comparisons and magic return values. That removes most of the surviving mutants, which were all in the old helpers. The `or -> and` mutant survived because a `TypeError` came from `len()` on a non-string instead. The tests now match the \"must be str\" message, and I added a case where both arguments are the wrong type.",
